6|0@bestofworldstar^1438533978#ctoz8g4:martyrfx$:Every membership card has a photo of the person who bought it. I went there with my brother and sister, but it was my dads card, and they wouldn't allow us to buy anything lol. But it's understandable. This was like 5 years ago too. If you live at the same address of the cardholder you can get one for free. It's a good place for groceries in "bulk". No assholes or cheapskates, just friendly people. The only bad time is going on a Saturday or Sunday midday. Everyone is there and it's hard to move with a big ass cart. Just say you're going to get some food at the cafe and you will be let in. I don't think you need membership for that.
