4|0@bestofworldstar^1438545884#ctp5of7:ole-gregg$:Kirkland brand (Costco's house brand) is consistently our go to. Their return policy is amazing. The employees don't hate their lives. I think it is well worth the membership.
2|0@bestofworldstar^1438629914#ctq84es:Bigpapajayy2$:Depends on what you buy, but generally you end up saving money. I use my membership a lot and I know other family and friends end up doing well at the end of the year. For me it is worth it because I have year round allergies and their generic brand of zyrtec is $15 for a 1 year supply, compared to name brand zyrtec which is $30 a month, that alone pays for the membership in savings 10 fold. You generally get the most savings on things that are marked up in regular grocery stores like soap, laundry detergent, razors, dental stuff, batteries, OTC medicine, coffee K cups, if you go with their brand. But a lot of their food is also priced well like chicken breast year round for ~2.80 per lb, rotisserie chickens for $5, baked goods are priced very well, bottled drinks, etc. Clothes are also cheap too, if you need things like socks/undershirts they are a good buy since those things are often getting dirty/sweaty/thrown out. You can't use a friends pass unless you go in with him, you can only give a membership card to one other family member who can go on his or her own.
